00:04:24.267 --> 00:04:27.227
Grid-tied homes can treat the utility as an infinite buffer,

00:04:27.727 --> 00:04:30.067
and that single-fact rewrites the storage math.

00:04:30.687 --> 00:04:36.987
An off-grid house has to balance panel output, battery capacity, and daily load with no fall back at all.

00:04:36.987 --> 00:04:44.067
conventional installs skip most of that over sizing because they can pull from the utility or push into it at any hour.

00:04:44.707 --> 00:04:49.267
Grid-tied owners can therefore size storage closer to one or two days of average use.

00:04:49.867 --> 00:04:54.527
Off-grid buyers lose that buffer and have to cover the longest expected outage window instead.

00:04:55.127 --> 00:05:00.707
Each extra power wall adds capital, plus the inverter and thermal hardware that ride along with it.

00:05:01.207 --> 00:05:05.787
That choice locks in higher upfront spending on batteries and the rest of the balance of system.

00:05:05.787 --> 00:05:11.287
The economics then shift from levelized cost of energy toward levelized cost of reliability.

00:05:11.887 --> 00:05:16.387
The marginal kilowatt hour of storage carries a much higher price tag under that rule.

00:05:17.027 --> 00:05:22.027
Oversizing also protects against consecutive low sun days, which is the point of the extra

00:05:22.027 --> 00:05:22.387
packs.

00:05:22.987 --> 00:05:27.827
The same storage to generation ratio runs well past what simple daily cycling would need.

00:05:28.487 --> 00:05:33.087
Tesla's Powerwall margins look better when buyers take smaller, cheaper banks that still

00:05:33.087 --> 00:05:34.047
cover most loads.

00:05:34.047 --> 00:05:39.407
modes. The showcase projects that create social proof demand the opposite. Big autonomous

00:05:39.407 --> 00:05:44.627
packages. Scaling the line depends on steering most customers toward daily cycle setups

00:05:44.627 --> 00:05:50.027
while still selling those premium packages. Large battery banks make sense in remote work,

00:05:50.387 --> 00:05:55.227
and they work against volume and suburbs where the grid is still there. That is a product design

00:05:55.227 --> 00:06:00.647
tension between attention-winning turnkey systems and the smaller, lower margin configs that

00:06:00.647 --> 00:06:05.927
would drive most unit sales. The off-grid slice may stay in niche that validates the hardware,

00:06:06.387 --> 00:06:10.507
while the wider residential market settles on hybrid setups with modest storage.

00:06:11.087 --> 00:06:15.467
A multi-packed bank is a heavy capital outlay even before roofwork and permitting.

00:06:16.027 --> 00:06:20.747
That total has to compete with simpler grid-tied alternatives that deliver most of the resilience

00:06:20.747 --> 00:06:26.527
for less money. High-attach rates in grid-connected homes with the long-autonomy kits reserved

00:06:26.527 --> 00:06:29.987
served for true off-grid customers would improve the margin mix.

00:06:30.527 --> 00:06:35.027
Most buyers will still pick a smaller footprint that covers evening peaks and short outages

00:06:35.027 --> 00:06:36.507
without paying the full premium.

00:06:37.247 --> 00:06:42.007
How cleanly Tesla splits those two offers will set how large residential storage can become.

00:06:42.747 --> 00:06:47.567
Vertical integration in cell and module production could eventually bend the cost curve for both

00:06:47.567 --> 00:06:49.387
grid tide and off-grid bundles.

00:06:49.927 --> 00:06:54.727
When that factory is at scale, the per kilowatt hour math of storage paired with on-site

00:06:54.727 --> 00:07:00.727
generation shifts again, and larger banks start to look sensible even in hybrid homes. Supply

00:07:00.727 --> 00:07:05.607
chain friction can hold those costs cuts back, and keep the premium configurations expensive

